@startuml Payment Processing with Webhook Handling
!theme plain
title Payment Processing with Webhook Handling\n(Async External Integration with Adapter Pattern)

' Participants
actor Customer as customer #LightBlue
participant "OrderController" as controller #E3F2FD
participant "OrderService" as orderService #E3F2FD
participant "PaymentService" as paymentService #E3F2FD
participant "GatewayResolver" as resolver #FFF3E0
participant "PaymentAdapter\n(Stripe)" as adapter #FFF3E0
participant "Payment Gateway\n(Stripe API)" as gateway #FFEBEE
database "Database" as db #E8F5E9
participant "PaymentWebhook\nController" as webhookController #E3F2FD
participant "EventSystem" as eventSystem #FCE4EC
participant "EmailService" as emailService #FCE4EC

' ===== PHASE 1: PAYMENT INITIATION =====
group Phase 1: Payment Initiation (Synchronous)
    customer -> controller: POST /api/v1/orders\n{checkout_token, payment_method: 'card'}
    activate controller
    
    controller -> orderService: createOrder(checkoutSession)
    activate orderService
    
    note over orderService
        **Order creation logic**
        - Validate checkout session
        - Lock stock (see Order Placement diagram)
        - Create order with status: 'pending_payment'
    end note
    
    orderService -> paymentService: initiatePayment(order)
    activate paymentService
    
    paymentService -> resolver: resolveAdapter('stripe')
    activate resolver
    note right of resolver
        **Gateway Resolution**
        Based on config:
        - payment.default_gateway = 'stripe'
        - payment.gateways.stripe.adapter = StripeAdapter::class
    end note
    resolver --> paymentService: StripeAdapter instance
    deactivate resolver
    
    paymentService -> db: INSERT INTO payments\n(order_id, method: 'card', status: 'initiated', amount, currency)
    db --> paymentService: payment.id = 1
    
    paymentService -> adapter: createPayment(paymentData)
    activate adapter
    note right of adapter
        **Payment Data Structure:**
        {
            "order_id": 123,
            "amount": 15000, // cents
            "currency": "usd",
            "success_url": "https://app.com/orders/123",
            "cancel_url": "https://app.com/checkout",
            "metadata": {
                "order_number": "ORD-20250101-001"
            }
        }
    end note
    
    adapter -> gateway: POST /v1/checkout/sessions\n{amount, currency, success_url, cancel_url}
    activate gateway
    gateway --> adapter: 201 Created\n{id: "cs_123xyz", url: "https://checkout.stripe.com/..."}
    deactivate gateway
    
    adapter --> paymentService: PaymentResponse\n{success: true, payment_id: "cs_123xyz", redirect_url: "..."}
    deactivate adapter
    
    paymentService -> db: UPDATE payments\nSET gateway_payment_id = 'cs_123xyz',\nredirect_url = '...',\ngateway_response = {...}
    db --> paymentService: Updated
    
    paymentService --> orderService: Payment {id: 1, redirect_url: "..."}
    deactivate paymentService
    
    orderService --> controller: Order {order_number: "ORD-20250101-001", redirect_url: "..."}
    deactivate orderService
    
    controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  {order, redirect_url},\n  'Order created, complete payment'\n)
    deactivate controller
    
    customer -> gateway: [Browser Redirect]\nGET https://checkout.stripe.com/...
    activate gateway
    note over customer, gateway
        **Customer on Stripe Checkout Page**
        User enters card details on Stripe's hosted page
    end note
end

' ===== PHASE 2: CUSTOMER PAYMENT =====
group Phase 2: Customer Payment (On Gateway)
    customer -> gateway: Submit card details
    gateway -> gateway: Process payment with card network
    note right of gateway
        Stripe communicates with:
        - Visa/Mastercard networks
        - Bank authorization
        - Fraud checks
    end note
    
    alt Payment Successful
        gateway --> customer: Payment confirmed\n[Redirect to success_url]
    else Payment Failed
        gateway --> customer: Payment failed\n[Show error, allow retry]
    end
    deactivate gateway
end

' ===== PHASE 3: WEBHOOK CALLBACK =====
group Phase 3: Webhook Callback (Asynchronous - Separate HTTP Request)
    note over gateway, webhookController
        **⏱ Time Gap: Typically 1-5 seconds after payment**
        This is a NEW HTTP request from Stripe to our server
    end note
    
    gateway ->> webhookController: POST /api/webhooks/payment/stripe\nStripe-Signature: t=...,v1=...\n{\n  "type": "checkout.session.completed",\n  "data": {"object": {"id": "cs_123xyz", ...}}\n}
    activate webhookController
    
    webhookController -> paymentService: processWebhook('stripe', request)
    activate paymentService
    
    ' Signature Verification
    paymentService -> adapter: verifyWebhookSignature(request)
    activate adapter
    adapter -> adapter: Calculate HMAC-SHA256\nusing webhook secret
    note right of adapter
        **Signature Verification:**
        - Extract timestamp and signature from header
        - Rebuild signed payload: timestamp + raw body
        - Calculate HMAC-SHA256 with secret key
        - Compare with provided signature
        
        **Security Critical:** Prevents malicious webhooks
    end note
    
    alt Signature Valid
        adapter --> paymentService: true
        deactivate adapter
        
        paymentService -> adapter: handleWebhook(request)
        activate adapter
        adapter -> adapter: Parse webhook payload
        adapter --> paymentService: WebhookResponse\n{event_type: 'payment.succeeded',\npayment_id: 'cs_123xyz',\nstatus: 'completed',\namount: 15000}
        deactivate adapter
        
        paymentService -> db: SELECT * FROM payments\nWHERE gateway_payment_id = 'cs_123xyz'
        db --> paymentService: Payment {id: 1, order_id: 123}
        
        alt Event = 'payment.succeeded'
            paymentService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
            activate db
            
            paymentService -> db: UPDATE payments\nSET status = 'paid',\npaid_at = NOW(),\ngateway_response = {...}
            
            paymentService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET payment_status = 'paid',\nstatus = 'confirmed',\nconfirmed_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = 123
            
            paymentService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(order_id, from_status, to_status, changed_by_type: 'system')
            
            paymentService -> db: COMMIT
            deactivate db
            
            paymentService -> eventSystem: dispatch('payment.completed',\n  payment, order)
            activate eventSystem
            note over eventSystem
                **Event Listeners:**
                - Send order confirmation email
                - Notify admin dashboard
                - Trigger analytics event
                - Update customer notification
            end note
            eventSystem ->> emailService: Send order confirmation
            deactivate eventSystem
            
            paymentService --> webhookController: WebhookResponse {status: 'processed'}
            
        else Event = 'payment.failed'
            paymentService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
            activate db
            
            paymentService -> db: UPDATE payments\nSET status = 'failed',\nfailed_at = NOW(),\nfailed_reason = '...'
            
            paymentService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET payment_status = 'failed',\nstatus = 'cancelled'
            
            paymentService -> db: COMMIT
            deactivate db
            
            paymentService -> orderService: releaseStock(order)
            note right
                Restore product quantities
                since order failed
            end note
            
            paymentService -> eventSystem: dispatch('payment.failed',\n  payment, reason)
            activate eventSystem
            eventSystem ->> emailService: Send payment failed notification
            deactivate eventSystem
            
            paymentService --> webhookController: WebhookResponse {status: 'processed'}
        end
        
        webhookController --> gateway: HTTP 200 OK\n{"received": true}
        note right of webhookController
            **Must return 200 immediately**
            Stripe retries if no 200 received
        end note
        deactivate paymentService
        deactivate webhookController
        
    else Signature Invalid
        adapter --> paymentService: false
        deactivate adapter
        
        paymentService -> paymentService: Log security warning
        note right of paymentService
            **Security Alert:**
            Potential malicious webhook attempt
            Log IP, payload, timestamp
        end note
        
        paymentService --> webhookController: Unauthorized
        deactivate paymentService
        
        webhookController --> gateway: HTTP 401 Unauthorized
        deactivate webhookController
    end
end

' ===== PHASE 4: CUSTOMER RETURN =====
group Phase 4: Customer Return to App
    note over customer
        Customer clicks "Return to merchant"
        or is auto-redirected
    end note
    
    customer -> controller: GET /orders/ORD-20250101-001
    activate controller
    
    controller -> orderService: getOrder('ORD-20250101-001')
    activate orderService
    
    orderService -> db: SELECT * FROM orders WHERE order_number = ?
    db --> orderService: Order {status: 'confirmed', payment_status: 'paid'}
    
    orderService --> controller: Order
    deactivate orderService
    
    controller --> customer: Order Confirmation Page\n✓ Payment successful\n✓ Order confirmed
    deactivate controller
end

' ===== ALTERNATIVE FLOWS =====
group Alternative: COD Payment (No Gateway)
    note over customer, controller
        If payment_method = 'cod', skip gateway entirely
    end note
    
    customer -> controller: POST /api/v1/orders {payment_method: 'cod'}
    controller -> orderService: createOrder(checkoutSession)
    orderService -> paymentService: initiatePayment(order)
    
    paymentService -> db: INSERT INTO payments\n(method: 'cod', status: 'cod_pending')
    
    paymentService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET status = 'confirmed',\npayment_status = 'cod_pending'
    
    paymentService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.confirmed', order)
    
    paymentService --> orderService: Payment {method: 'cod', no redirect}
    orderService --> controller: Order {status: 'confirmed'}
    controller --> customer: Order confirmed\nPay on delivery
end

' Notes
note over gateway, webhookController
    **Webhook Retry Logic:**
    Stripe automatically retries webhooks if:
    - No response received within 30 seconds
    - Non-200 status code returned
    
    Retry schedule: immediately, 1h, 3h, 6h, 12h, 24h
    
    **Idempotency:** Our webhook handler must handle duplicate events
    Check payment status before processing to prevent double-updates
end note

note over paymentService, adapter
    **Adapter Pattern Benefits:**
    - Switch payment gateways without changing business logic
    - Easy to add new gateways (PayPal, Razorpay, etc.)
    - Centralized gateway configuration
    - Consistent interface for all payment methods
    
    **To add new gateway:**
    1. Implement PaymentAdapterInterface
    2. Add config: payment.gateways.paypal.adapter = PayPalAdapter::class
    3. No changes to PaymentService code
end note

@enduml
